# Training Compound on a later turn with a basic land: it entered on turn 1, but on turn 3 Bot1 has played an Island, a basic land
# (CR 205.4a), so "if you control a basic land" holds and the Compound taps for {G} (the second half of the condition; the
# refusal of the same ability without the Island is the other scenario). Red is on offer too.

[Bot1 Deck]
Training Compound
Island
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Training Compound.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Training Compound.Activate(Ability: {R} or {G}; Color: Green)

[Expect]
Bot1.Mana = {G}
Bot1.Battlefield.Training Compound.Tapped = true
